'''velvet''' (vel′vet), ''v.'' [< ''velvet'', ''n.''] '''I.''' ''intrans.'' To produce velvet-painting.
{{smaller block|Verditure . . . is the palest green that is, but good to ''velvet'' upon black in any drapery.
{{right|''Peacham'', Drawing.}}}}

'''II.''' ''trans.'' To cover with velvet; cause to resemble velvet. [Rare.]

'''velvetbreast''' (vel′vet-brest), ''n.'' The American merganser or sheldrake, ''Mergus americanus.'' [Connecticut.]

'''velvet-bur''' (vel′vet-bėr), ''n.'' See ''Priva.''

